    },
    {
      "line": 17,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "scene 005.1 — the first pyramid collapse"
    },
    {
      "line": 19,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "scene meta:"
    },
    {
      "line": 20,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "location: Desert beach / pyramid site"
    },
    {
      "line": 21,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "time: year 15"
    },
    {
      "line": 22,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "participants: Vairis, Senareth, Elyraen, burnt-red Giants"
    },
    {
      "line": 23,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "focus: The first 50ft sandstone step-pyramid collapses due to thermal expansion, but the Giants and Nephoretti analyze the failure data to refine future construction."
    },
    {
      "line": 24,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "continuity: Fifteen years after the Day 0 landing; follows the convergence and settlement established in chapter 004"
    },
    {
      "line": 25,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "presentation: undecided"
    },
    {
      "line": 27,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The first pyramid collapsed on a morning that had started with such promise."
    },
    {
      "line": 29,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Vairis and a cluster of desert Giants had been working for three months on the structure—layering sandstone blocks in a step-pyramid formation that was supposed to amplify vrill-resonance through geometric progression."
    },
    {
      "line": 30,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The theory was sound."
    },
    {
      "line": 31,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The mathematics checked."
    },
    {
      "line": 32,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The consciousness-touch techniques were properly applied."
    },
    {
      "line": 34,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The execution was catastrophic."
    },
    {
      "line": 36,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The collapse started at the base—one block shifting fractionally as desert heat expanded the stone unevenly."
    },
    {
      "line": 37,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "That shift propagated upward through fifty vertical feet of carefully stacked architecture, each layer magnifying the instability of the one below."
    },
    {
      "line": 38,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "For a moment, the entire structure seemed to hang suspended, geometry fighting gravity, vrill-binding struggling to maintain cohesion against physical reality."
    },
    {
      "line": 40,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Then it fell."
    },
    {
      "line": 42,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The sound was like thunder compressed into a single point—crack of stone against stone multiplied by hundreds of tons of falling mass."
    },
    {
      "line": 43,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Dust exploded outward in a wave that temporarily obscured the sun."
    },
    {
      "line": 44,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Giants scattered, their massive forms surprisingly nimble when survival required it."
    },
    {
      "line": 45,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Nephoretti dove for cover behind surviving structures or simply threw themselves flat against sand and hoped the debris wouldn't reach them."
    },
    {
      "line": 47,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "When the dust settled, Vairis emerged coughing, their practical nature already assessing damage."
    },
    {
      "line": 48,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Three Nephoretti injured but alive."
    },
    {
      "line": 49,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "No Giants hurt—their stone-flesh could withstand impacts that would obliterate smaller beings."
    },
    {
      "line": 50,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And where the pyramid had stood, now only rubble remained, scattered across two hundred yards of desert beach."
    },
    {
      "line": 52,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "Vairis",
      "text": "\"Expansion coefficient miscalculation,\""
    },
    {
      "line": 54,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "Senareth",
      "text": "\"So we adjust,\""
    },
    {
      "line": 56,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The burnt-red Giants who had been primary builders gathered around the ruins, their rumbling harmonics clearly expressing disappointment."
    },
    {
      "line": 57,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "But one of them—the tall sandstone-textured Giant who had first approached Olythae's art—knelt and began reshaping the debris."
    },
    {
      "line": 58,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Not clearing it, but studying it."
    },
    {
      "line": 59,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Their consciousness-touch explored how the stones had fractured, where the stress-points had accumulated, what the failure itself could teach about geometry and resonance."
    },
    {
      "line": 61,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "Elyraen",
      "text": "\"They're not discouraged,\""
    },
    {
      "line": 63,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It became the pattern for the next eight decades."
    },
    {
      "line": 65,
      "type": "scene_header",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "line": 67,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "year 47"
    }
  ],
